---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Contact from "../components/Contact.astro";
import PersonSchema from "../components/PersonSchema.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Victoria Adler – Actor"
  description="Swedish actor based in London, trained at Stockholm Art School and the Kogan Academy of Dramatic Arts, with a background in stage combat, archery and dance."
  path="/"
  ogType="profile"
  preloads={[
    "lora-latin.woff2",
    "cabin-700-latin.woff2",
    "roboto-400-latin.woff2",
  ]}
  outfit
  siteBase
  brandHref="#"
  bodyId="page-top"
>
  <PersonSchema slot="head" />
  <div class="header-container">
    <div class="video-container">
      <video
        class="responsive-video"
        preload="auto"
        autoplay
        loop
        muted
        playsinline
        poster="assets/video/vid 1.webp"
      >
        <source src="assets/video/12-2024-header-1920.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <div class="scroll-down-arrow">
        <i class="fa fa-arrow-down"></i>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="text-center content-section" id="about">
    <h1>
      <b>Victoria Adler</b>
    </h1>
    <h3 style="font-family: Outfit, sans-serif; margin-bottom: 2.5%;">actor</h3>
    <div class="row">
      <!-- 3rd quote -->
      <div class="col-md">
        <figure
          class="bg-grey p-3 rounded"
          style="border-left: .5rem solid #ffffff;"
        >
          <blockquote class="blockquote pb-2">
            <p>
              "Victoria Adler’s performance in her numerous roles is in such
              contrast to one another that it seems like she’s an entirely new
              person every time she comes onstage."
            </p>
            <p>
              <b>"Her Macduff is practically award-winning;</b> a rather basic
              and forgettable character usually, Adler shows us the hell hath no
              fury beneath the character’s usual stoic manner."
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="blockquote-footer mb-0 font-italic">
            Katerina Partolina Schwartz, Perpper & Salt, 14th August 2024
          </figcaption>
          <a
            href="https://pepperandsalt.uk/2024/08/14/macbeth-sleep-no-more/"
            class="btn review grey darken-4"
          >
            Read Review
          </a>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <!-- 2nd quote -->
      <div class="col-md">
        <figure
          class="bg-grey p-3 rounded"
          style="border-left: .5rem solid #ffffff;"
        >
          <blockquote class="blockquote pb-2">
            <p>
              "Victoria Adler (First Witch, Macduff and a very engaging Doctor)
              differentiates her main and subsidiary characters with great
              skill, subtle changes in posture and voice ensuring you know just
              who she is playing at what point."
            </p>
            <p>
              "The stage tension between Floyd and Adler was electric as they
              circled each other like a pair of prize fighters preparing to go
              the distance. Verbally it was superb. Physically, it was
              breathtaking. Peerless."
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="blockquote-footer mb-0 font-italic">
            Tim Wilcock, FringeReview, 9th August 2023
          </figcaption>
          <a
            href="http://fringereview.co.uk/review/edinburgh-fringe/2023/macbeth-sleep-no-more/"
            class="btn review grey darken-4"
          >
            Read Review
          </a>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md">
        <!-- First quote -->
        <figure
          class="bg-grey p-3 rounded"
          style="border-left: .5rem solid #ffffff;"
        >
          <blockquote class="blockquote pb-2">
            <p>
              <br />
              <br />
              "... but none shines brighter than Victoria Adler, who is
              scintillating in whichever body she is inhabiting. Adler’s sword
              fighting scene with Amy Floyd’s Macbeth is one of the highlights
              of the whole show..."
              <br />
              <br />
              <br />
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="blockquote-footer mb-0 font-italic">
            Greg Holstead, North West End UK, 10th August 2023
          </figcaption>
          <a
            href="https://northwestend.com/macbeth-sleep-no-more-the-space-niddrie-street/"
            class="btn review grey darken-4"
          >
            Read Review
          </a>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-sm">
        <img
          class="headshot"
          alt="Victoria Adler headshot by David Yiu, 2024"
          src="assets/img/headshot 2024/q1/victoria-adler-10.webp"
        />

        <br />
        <br />
        <!-- <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm ">
                    <div class="card mx-auto" style="width: 18rem; color: black;">
                        <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="card-img-top" src="assets/img/ticket_pic/chrismas_charol.webp" alt="Card image cap">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5 class="card-title">A Christmas Carol</h5>
                            <a href="https://www.ticketsource.co.uk/shadowroad" class="btn btn grey darken-2">Tickets</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
               <div class="col-sm ">
                    <div class="card mx-auto" style="width: 18rem; color: black;">
                        <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="card-img-top" src="assets/img/ticket_pic/2023MACBETJ_AYK.webp" alt="Card image cap">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5 class="card-title">Macbeth</h5>
