                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div> -->
        <!-- </div>   -->
      </div>
      <div class="col-sm text-main order-sm-first">
        <p>
          <br />
          Victoria Adler, a Swedish actor from the small town of Enköping. From
          her formative years, she immersed herself fully in narratives, whether
          films or books. She often daydreamed about the lives of the various
          characters. Little did she know this was the spark to her interest in
          acting. Over time, films like "The Lord of the Rings," "Troy," "The
          Last Samurai," and "Gladiator" not only captured her imagination but
          also ignited her fascination with swordsmanship. Additionally, BBC's
          rendition of "Robin Hood" came along and prompted her exploration of
          archery and historical reenactment.
          <br />
          <br />
          At 15, Victoria discovered that acting was the gateway to
          participating in these captivating narratives. Her role as Juliet in
          Shakespeare's "Romeo and Juliet" marked her stage debut and propelled
          her forward without a moment's hesitation. Subsequently, this led her
          to audition to the acting program at Stockholm Art School (2010-2013),
          where she got accepted. Alongside her studies, Victoria entered the
          world of film. From roles in short films to numerous appearances as an
          extra. This opened up her eyes to the profession and she never looked
          back. She was determined to become a part of it. The next move was
          relocating to Boston, MA after graduating. Where she worked as an Au
          Pair while pursuing acting studies at JRP New England.
          <br />
          <br />
          After a few years of gaining life experience, she started to audition
          for a number of drama schools. She secured a spot at The School of the
          Science of Acting (Kogan Academy of Dramatic Arts) 2017. This brought
          her to London and the city that has been her main base for the last 7
          years. Graduating into a very different industry in 2020, Victoria has
          since then embodied several roles on stage and in front of the camera.
          <br />
          <br />
          At present, Victoria is coaching archery at Archery Fit as well as
          improving her skills and knowledge. Coming from a physical background,
          encompassing football, horse riding and dance, she thrives in
          physically demanding roles.
          <br />
          She is also working as an acting coach alongside auditioning and
          working on her craft.
          <br />
          <br />
          Representation and professional collaboration offers are welcome.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Contact />
</BaseLayout>
